-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a6543beb-6274-5718-8d3e-e912b570d07d
-- title:
--   Ordinary unit-root refinement at level Nrp: witness existence
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete with respect to its maximal ideal) with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and $p$ is a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $(p:\mathcal O)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$.
--
--   **Residual representation.** $\bar\rho$ is a residual Galois representation over $k$: a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $\bar\rho.V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(\bar\rho.V)$ which is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Hypothesis `habs` asserts absolute irreducibility: after base change to $\overline k$, every subspace stable under all $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ is $\bot$ or $\top$. Hypothesis `hord` asserts that the adic representation [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep ρbar`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196) (the same data regarded over the local ring $k$) is ordinary at $p$: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $(p)\in P.\mathrm{nonunits}$ there is a submodule $L\subseteq\bar\rho.V$ spanned by the first vector of a basis, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, and with $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)v-v\in L$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$.
--
--   **Levels and ramification bookkeeping.** $S$ is a finite set of primes (`hS`) containing $p$ (`hpS`); $N$ is a nonzero natural number with $p\nmid N$ (`hpN`) all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$ (`hNS`), and $Np$ is nonzero. $S_{\min}\subseteq S$ contains $p$, and for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ if and only if $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (`hmin`, where unramifiedness at $q$ means $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)=1$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of any valuation subring over $q$); every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N$ (`hNmin`); every prime $q\neq p$ outside $S_{\min}$ which divides $N$ divides $N$ to order at least two (`hNunr`); and for each $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, the representation attached to $\bar\rho$ is unipotent on inertia at $q$, i.e. $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma))=(X-1)^2$ for $\sigma$ in inertia at any valuation subring over $q$ (`htame`).
--
--   **Auxiliary prime.** $r$ is a prime with $r\geq 5$, $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$ and $p\nmid r-1$. Hypothesis `hrρ` is the absence of level raising at $r$: for every valuation subring $P$ over $r$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$ (that is, $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup and acts on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^r$), $\mathrm{tr}(\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma))^2\neq (r+1)^2$ in $k$.
--
--   **Residual eigensystems and their points.** Under the standing assumptions that weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(Np)$ and on $\Gamma_0(N)$ admit integral structures (the $\mathbb Z$-lattice of forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients spans over $\mathbb C$), $\theta_1$ and $\theta_0$ are ring homomorphisms to $k$ from the Hecke algebras [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra (N*p) 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) and [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebras of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\nmid$ level, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ with $q\mid$ level, $q\notin S$). Hypotheses `hθ₁` and `hθ₀` say that these characters match the traces of $\bar\rho$: for every prime $\ell\notin S$ not dividing $Np$ (respectively $N$), every valuation subring $P$ over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$,
--   $$\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta_i(T_\ell)X+\ell .$$
--   Further, $\pi_{T_0}$ and $\pi_{T_1}$ are $\mathcal O$-algebra maps to $\mathcal O$ from the local Hecke algebras [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal (N*p) S 𝒪 θ₁`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (localisations of the base-changed Hecke lattice algebras at the prime complement of the kernel of the relevant character), and `hπ` asserts that they agree on the away-from-level Hecke operators: for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid Np$ and $\ell\nmid N$, $\pi_{T_1}(\pi(T_\ell))=\pi_{T_0}(\pi(T_\ell))$.
--
--   **The level-$Nr$ corner.** $H_0\leq(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ is the subgroup of those $v$ whose image in $\mathbb Z/r$ is $1$ (`hH₀`). $\mathbb T_0$ is a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and acts on $H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)=\mathrm{Hom}(\mathrm{Additive}\,\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr),\mathcal O)$ compatibly with the $\mathcal O$-action. $S_0$ is an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T_0$ (finitely many complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$, maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals, with $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j$ exactly when $i\neq j$), $i_0$ an index, and $e_0$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism from the corner ring $S_0.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ onto [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131); the corner module $e_{i_0}\cdot H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)$ is finite and free over $\mathcal O$. An element $t_p$ of the corner ring is given, together with:
--
--   - `hT₀`: for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\nmid Nr$, the element $e_0^{-1}(\pi(T_\ell))$ acts on the corner module as the Hecke operator `heckeT (N*r) H₀ ℓ 𝒪`;
--
--   - `htp`: $t_p$ is a unit and acts on the corner module both as `heckeT (N*r) H₀ p 𝒪` and as `heckeTlower (N*r) H₀ p 𝒪`;
--
--   - `hocc₀`: the submodule of the corner module annihilated by the kernel of $\pi_{T_0}\circ e_0$ is nonzero;
--
--   - `hrk₀`: the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner module equals the rank of that annihilated submodule times the rank of the corner ring;
--
--   - `hgen`: every $t\in\mathbb T_0$ acts on $H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)$ as some element of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the range of [`CohCarrier.opFamily (N*r) H₀ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) (the family sending a generator $T_\ell$ or $U_q$ to `heckeTL` at that prime, and $\langle d\rangle$ to `diamondL`);
--
--   - a guarded Hecke family: $t_{\mathrm{full}}:\mathrm{Gen}(Nr,S)\to\mathbb T_0$ and $c_{\mathrm{full}}:\mathrm{Gen}(Nr,S)\to\mathcal O$ such that, for every generator $g$ satisfying the guard that $g=U_q$ only when $q\mid N$ (no constraint for $T$-generators and diamonds), $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ acts as `opFamily` at $g$ (`htfull`) and $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c_{\mathrm{full}}(g)\in S_0.\mathfrak m\,i_0$ (`hcfull`);
--
--   - `hcofull` (co-fullness): any $v\in H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)$ such that for each guarded $g$ and each $k$ some power $(t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c_{\mathrm{full}}(g))^n$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k\cdot H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)$ already lies in the corner module;
--
--   - `hfaith₀`: the corner ring acts faithfully on the corner module;
--
--   - `hdia`: for every $\sigma\in\Gamma_0(Nr)$, the diamond operator `diamondRaw (N*r) H₀ 𝒪 σ` fixes every element of the corner module.
--
--   **Unit root.** Finally $\tilde\alpha$ is an element of $S_0.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ which is a unit, satisfies $\tilde\alpha^2-t_p\tilde\alpha+p=0$, and satisfies $\tilde\alpha-t_p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}\cdot S_0.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ (the image of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exist: the nonvanishing of $Nrp$; a subgroup $H\leq(\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times$ equal to the preimage of $H_0$ under `ZMod.unitsMap` for $Nr\mid Nrp$; commutative rings $\mathbb T_a$ and $\mathbb T_1$, each an $\mathcal O$-algebra acting on $H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ compatibly with the $\mathcal O$-action and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module; an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\iota:\mathbb T_a\to\mathbb T_1$ with $\iota(t)\cdot v=t\cdot v$ for all $t$ and $v$; an element $U\in\mathbb T_1$ acting on $H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ as `heckeT (N*r*p) H p 𝒪`, with $\mathcal O[\,\mathrm{range}\,\iota\cup\{U\}\,]=\mathbb T_1$; idempotent splittings $S_a$ of $\mathbb T_a$ with index $i_a$ and $S_1$ of $\mathbb T_1$ with index $i_1$, both corner modules being finite and free over $\mathcal O$; a level datum `LevelLE (N*r*p) (N*r*p) ⊤ H 1`; and maps $t_A:\mathrm{Gen}(Nr,S)\to\mathbb T_a$, $d_A:(\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times\to\mathbb T_a$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   With the guard that $T$-generators are unrestricted, $U_q$-generators are admitted only when $q\mid N$, and diamond generators are excluded:
--
--   1. for every guarded $g$, $t_A(g)$ acts on $H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ as `heckeT (N*r*p) H ℓ 𝒪` for $g=T_\ell$ and as `heckeT (N*r*p) H q 𝒪` for $g=U_q$ (the diamond branch, which would act as the identity, is excluded by the guard);
--
--   2. for every guarded $g$, $t_A(g)-c_{\mathrm{full}}(g)\in S_a.\mathfrak m\,i_a$;
--
--   3. for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times$, $d_A(d)$ acts as `diamondL (N*r*p) H 𝒪 d`;
--
--   4. for every $d$, $d_A(d)-1\in S_a.\mathfrak m\,i_a$;
--
--   5. $\mathcal O[\,t_A(\text{guarded generators})\cup\mathrm{range}\,d_A\,]=\mathbb T_a$;
--
--   6. the contraction of $S_1.\mathfrak m\,i_1$ along $\iota$ is $S_a.\mathfrak m\,i_a$, and $U\notin S_1.\mathfrak m\,i_1$;
--
--   7. for every $a\in\mathcal O$: if $\tilde\alpha-a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $S_0.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$, then $U-a\in S_1.\mathfrak m\,i_1$;
--
--   8. the corner submodule of $S_1$ at $i_1$ is contained in the corner submodule of $S_a$ at $i_a$;
--
--   9. both corner submodules are nonzero;
--
--   10. $\mathbb T_a$ and $\mathbb T_1$ act faithfully on $H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$, and $S_1.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_1$ acts faithfully on its corner submodule;
--
--   11. there exist $t^1_{\mathrm{full}}:\mathrm{Gen}(Nrp,S)\to\mathbb T_1$ and $c^1_{\mathrm{full}}:\mathrm{Gen}(Nrp,S)\to\mathcal O$ with the following properties. For every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid Nrp$ and $\ell\nmid Nr$, $t^1_{\mathrm{full}}(T_\ell)=\iota(t_A(T_\ell))$ and $c^1_{\mathrm{full}}(T_\ell)=c_{\mathrm{full}}(T_\ell)$. For every prime $q$ with $q\mid Nrp$, $q\mid Nr$ and $q\mid N$, $t^1_{\mathrm{full}}(U_q)=\iota(t_A(U_q))$ and $c^1_{\mathrm{full}}(U_q)=c_{\mathrm{full}}(U_q)$. For the generator $U_p$ one has $t^1_{\mathrm{full}}(U_p)=U$ and $\tilde\alpha-c^1_{\mathrm{full}}(U_p)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $S_0.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$, so that $c^1_{\mathrm{full}}(U_p)$ lifts the residue of the unit root. For every $d$, $t^1_{\mathrm{full}}(\langle d\rangle)=\iota(d_A(d))$ and $c^1_{\mathrm{full}}(\langle d\rangle)=1$. Moreover, writing the level-$Nrp$ guard as: $g=U_q$ (for a prime $q\mid Nrp$) only if $q\mid Np$, every $x\in\mathbb T_1$ acts on $H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ as some element of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the image under [`CohCarrier.opFamily (N*r*p) H S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) of the guarded generators; for every guarded $g$, $t^1_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ acts as `opFamily` at $g$ and $t^1_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c^1_{\mathrm{full}}(g)\in S_1.\mathfrak m\,i_1$; and co-fullness holds at level $Nrp$: any $v\in H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ such that for each guarded $g$ and each $k$ there is $n$ with $(t^1_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c^1_{\mathrm{full}}(g))^n\cdot v\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k\cdot H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ lies in the corner submodule of $S_1$ at $i_1$.
--
--   This is the passage from level $Nr$ to level $Nrp$ in the ordinary case: it produces, out of a corner of the Hecke action on $H^1$ at level $Nr$ identified with the local Hecke algebra of the residual eigensystem $\theta_0$, a pair of Hecke algebras at level $Nrp$ together with an idempotent corner refined at the unit root $\tilde\alpha$ of $X^2-t_pX+p$, carrying occupancy, faithfulness and fullness of the refined corner. It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_cornerData_unitRoot_refinement_package_level_mul_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_cornerData_unitRoot_refinement_package_level_mul_of_not_cube_dvd), which packages these witnesses into the corner-ring identification at level $Nrp$.
